WEBVTT

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.410
Hey, it's morning, Big Sister.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.040
Is it really that time already?

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.290
I'll have natto with green onions this morning.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.200
Did you fight with your boyfriend again?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.620
Boyfriend? Did I have one of those?

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.200
That wasn't obvious or anything.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.870
I don't mind you sleeping over,
but how many times has this happened?

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.500
Can you go to work like this?

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.080
Wow, this is so cool!
You got another article printed in the paper!

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:02.410
"Ayaka Tachikawa of 22/7
reflects on her last year with enthusiasm."

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.200
Wow, you pulled the wool over their eyes!

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.040
I'm an idol, so that's normal.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.000
There are fans of yours at my company.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.330
When I told them that you were my sister,
they spilled their coffee.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.700
Stop spreading rumors.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.290
I started because I thought
it might be good material for a manga,

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.160
not to continue it as a career.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.080
What? Let me have one thing
to take pride in my sister in!

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.580
It's still pretty awesome
you got into the Internet news.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.830
Thanks.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.120
Your bag.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.370
Thanks!

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.500
But you've been working so hard,
I'm seeing you in a new light now.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.790
That day you said you wanted to become
a manga artist and ran off, I was worried.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.000
It's admirable!

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.830
Ugh, so creepy.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.250
Okay, I'm off.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.250
If you're gonna make up with him,
get some sexy undies.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.200
You dummy.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:51.910
I may as well get going, too.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.750
"Lullaby of the Stars"

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:32.120
Soon it will be one year since 22/7 debuted
and became the talk of the town.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.410
They were chosen
for the Japan Record Fine Arts Award

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.830
in the Best Newcomer category.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.000
One could say they're quite a force, 22/7!

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.660
Their new single has just been announced.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.080
Okay!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.750
Ayaka.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.950
Morning, Christer.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.870
Do you remember all the moves
for the new song?

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.040
I'm still learning.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.000
Same here. I haven't completely
memorized the choreography yet.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.700
Hey, isn't that Miu Takigawa?

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.750
The one from 22/7?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.620
And next to her is Ayaka Tachikawa.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.450
--Seriously?
--You want to talk to them?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.910
I'm too embarrassed! You do it!

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.290
Come on. We're getting on.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.540
We have work until tonight again, right?

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.660
Being an idol is all about being exploited.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.910
It feels weird, somehow.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:29.700
I can see that.
Your debut was pretty spectacular, after all.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.250
I have come here
to do the job I want to do the least.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.750
Well? Have you come
to like being an idol at all?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.750
I love everyone. But...

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:40.950
But?

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.330
There are still a lot of things
I don't think I'm suited towards,

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.950
and I can't be as bold as you are.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.830
Is this where I really belong?

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.870
I guess I really haven't thought about it,
whether or not this is where I belong.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.660
"'I' - 'I'
'ONE'"

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.700
"'I' - 'I'
'ONE'"

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.700
The kanji for "where one belongs"
is an ideogram,

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.000
one that looks like a hard helmet
upon someone sitting.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.950
Because "where one belongs"
is a place you sit when you're tired.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.660
It's like a field or a moor.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.750
It's not something that's to be decided.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.870
It's more important that you stopped here
when you got tired, right?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.290
Let's go, Christer.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.540
Okay.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:39.120
"12 YEARS AGO"

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.370
"12 YEARS AGO"

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.370
Ayane and Ayana got Bu all dirty!

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.080
We didn't do anything.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.580
We didn't do anything!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.910
That's a lie! You threw Bu!

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:55.540
The three Tachikawa sisters
were famous in the neighborhood.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:06:00.910
We would go to the park, and they took
every opportunity they had to make me cry.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.160
Hey! Ayana! Ayane!
Did you apologize to Ayaka properly?

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.750
Yeah, we did.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.950
You liars!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.160
One thing I hated was my sisters.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.080
Mom, sing the song about the stars?

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.750
One thing I loved
were the lullabies my mother sang to me.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:25.000
♪ The first star sparkled ♪

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.120
♪ The second star twinkled ♪

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:36.000
--♪ The third star glittered ♪
--And there was one more thing I loved.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.620
Oh, that book.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.450
I'm still reading it!

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.370
Shut up. It's my book, isn't it?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.500
I hate you! I wish you didn't exist!

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.000
Hey, wait a second, Ayane!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.410
Ayaka's too much of a crybaby.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:07.370
Nuh-uh! I am not a crybaby!
It's their fault for being so mean to me!

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.080
You know that your big sisters love you, right?

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.160
That's why they're meddling in everything.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.580
That's not true! They're always mean to me!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.870
I hate you.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.830
Hey, Ayane!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.200
Ayane said she hates me!
She said she hates me!

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:31.750
Mom, sing the star song!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:37.410
♪ The third star glittered ♪

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:43.290
♪ The fourth star dazzled ♪

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.040
A one-year anniversary concert?

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.290
Yes. It's been decided
that a large-scale concert

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:51.410
for your formation day
will be held on December 24th.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.540
Wow! An anniversary!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.950
Amazing!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.580
It's already been a year, huh?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.290
So it's been decided
that 22/7 is one year old, then.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.120
Goo goo!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.790
It's one year. That's so cute!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.660
Kids shouldn't coddle other kids!

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.700
I'm not a kid!

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.910
So that means it's been year since we met.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.250
Thinking about it,
it did go by in the blink of an eye.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.450
For our anniversary concert, it makes you
want to do something spectacular.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.830
A live broadcast concert
from Mount Fuji's summit!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.870
Moron. The air would be too thin for that.
You wanna die?

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:24.830
Fuji is in the same league as Everest.
It's too dangerous.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.500
It was just a joke.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.330
--I'm looking forward to the setlist.
--Right.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:35.000
As we approach the anniversary concert,
promotion and your lessons will get more busy.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.450
This particular Order is about recreation
before the concert.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.410
"This"?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.160
"DECEMBER 24th
ONE YEAR ANNIVERSARY LIVE CONCERT"

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.160
A one-night, two-day trip
to a hot spring in Hakone, the Hoshimi Villa.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.120
"A ONE-NIGHT, TWO-DAY TRIP TO A HOT SPRING
IN HAKONE, THE HOSHIMI VILLA."

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.120
A one-night, two-day trip
to a hot spring in Hakone, the Hoshimi Villa.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.580
Hooray!

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:56.200
Wow, it's so pretty!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.540
Thank you for coming.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.370
Thank you for having us.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.200
Thanks!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.450
Hey! Greet them properly!

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.910
Jun, don't run!

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.790
We take off our shoes
and put on these slippers.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:11.160
Thanks! It sure is different from a hotel, huh!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:18.410
--This is our first trip together, isn't it?
--It seems like we should be able to relax here.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.660
What, you got an objection?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.080
Shut the hell up! Take it back!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.540
What? You're so weak,
you better not pick a fight with us!

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:37.160
Ayane? A fight? With three boys?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.790
You're too uppity!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.040
S-Stop!

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.080
I won't let you bully Ayane!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.830
Ayaka!

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.700
Being protected by her little sister? Lame!

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.500
Just what is a first grader
gonna be able to do, huh?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.290
Hey!

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:19.290
Did my little sisters do something?

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:22.000
Aw, crap! She's a sixth grader. Run!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.040
Ayana!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.580
I was so scared!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:31.200
Just what the heck were you two doing?
You two really are too much.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.870
B-But...

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:36.410
To begin with, Ayane,
why were you fighting with boys?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.580
But...

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.830
...they were calling Ayaka weak!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:47.040
Ayane, I thought you hated me.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:53.160
Sheesh... You're both dummies.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:58.500
It doesn't matter whether we love or hate
each other! Because we're sisters!

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:14.580
After that, the fights Ayane and I
had mysteriously disappeared.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.540
Wow!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.950
It's so threatening.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.620
It's pretty lavish.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.540
Whew, it's so generous.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:29.120
Hey, can we eat it? Can we?

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.370
Thanks for the meal!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.830
It's so good!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.000
Yummy!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.830
I-It's so good!

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.540
This fatty meat is really delicious!

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.580
What kind of sashimi do you all like?

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.410
Hmm, the lean kind.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.830
Salmon roe! Salmon roe!

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:45.790
I love shrimp!

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.660
I prefer shellfish.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.370
S-Salmon.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.160
Nicorun?

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.700
I like sea urchin.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:56.290
Dang, you have high-class taste!
As expected of ya!

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.500
How adult!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.620
But sea urchin is kind of strange.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.000
What part of it?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.250
How they can swim with that kind of body,
yet out of the ocean, they dissolve.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.500
Delicious.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:15.700
W-Wait a sec! What did she just say?
I didn't quite hear her.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.370
She just said they swim.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:20.660
She seems to be under the impression
that sea urchins are fish.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.200
There are really folks like that?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.750
Unbelievable!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:24.830
And I liked them, too.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:26.540
I'm so scared!

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:28.580
Funny! You're joking, right?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.950
Nicorun, you're funny!

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.500
Huh? What?

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.290
Oh, heck. She wasn't kidding after all.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:38.330
I-It's not her fault!
She's just an ordinary idol.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.160
Hey, leader, you tell her.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.750
I can't! She's not putting out
welcoming vibes right now!

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:45.660
This is so scary!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.790
It's so strange.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.750
Looks delicious.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.500
That was so good!

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:03.500
After your meal,
how does an open-air bath sound?

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.120
"FEMALE OPEN-AIR
STAR-GAZING BATH"

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.120
An open-air bath?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.580
Bath time, bath time!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.870
An open-air bath in the fall
seems kind of stylish.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.200
I wonder if there are monkeys?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.790
There might be.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.000
Seriously? Are you serious?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.540
I wonder if bears will show up, too.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.540
I'm scared of bears.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.750
Ayaka? Ayaka?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.620
Hm? What?

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.120
What are you doing?

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.250
Nothing, really.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:32.500
That math teacher just now,
he was super creepy, wasn't he?

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.750
Not really. That's normal.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.450
Isn't Fukukawa from Class 3 super cute?

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.000
He's normal, too.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.370
Ayaka's got a bad vibe to her, doesn't she?

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:45.870
She's kinda a loser.

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.750
It's like she sees
everyone in the world as an idiot.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:50.870
I get that, too.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.910
In school, I was alone much of the time.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.750
Because of our ages, my sisters
were in different middle and high schools.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:03.250
When it came to gossip or who was hot,
I didn't really care about any of that.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:08.950
Huh?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.410
Hey. Is it true you dumped Fukukawa?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.200
He's super depressed.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.750
Just how cute do you think you are?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.500
I feel bad for him.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.080
Lame.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:28.450
Why am I going to school, again?

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.200
I started drawing manga in middle school.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:39.410
My first completed work drew the attention
of an editor, who contacted me.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:46.080
I started living by myself
in spring quarter of my sophomore year.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:51.120
As I got more manga work,
I started going to school part-time.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.250
As long as I graduated,
my parents were happy.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.160
That was their one condition.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.000
They have a keen eye.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.750
So big! We're the only ones here.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.660
Man, this feels good.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.200
Just like Hoshimi Villas' name says,
you can see so many pretty stars.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.200
Meow!

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.410
Hold on. Is it okay
to bring Mr. Wall in with us?

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:25.040
Sure, it is. He's just
a stuffed animal, after all.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.620
Just remember your manners.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.620
Did you say, "Just a stuffed animal"?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.370
Are you really wearing your glasses
during a bath?

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.790
My eyesight is bad.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:35.500
But you can't even see in front of you.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.950
This feels so good.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.200
Yeah.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.000
It's so strange.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:49.200
The eight of us were gathered from all over,
but we've spent a year together like this.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:55.660
Seriously, I was wondering how this
was gonna go at first, but it's been fun.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.500
Mr. Wall wasn't so bad after all!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.040
He even came in the bath with us!

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.540
And it appears that we've acquired
some stamina as well.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.080
Well, I guess we get passing marks.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:10.200
We've done our best this whole time.
What will we do next?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.910
If we're able to become stars
like the ones above us...

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:16.660
I can feel it.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:20.500
After that concert we had a little while ago,
we've started to become one.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.540
That's how I feel.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.160
Revolution!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.370
Again?

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.870
How many times has it been for you?

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.040
This is the fourth time.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.750
Lots of revolutions!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:34.830
Hold up. Who cut the cards?

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:37.620
But isn't it more fun
the more revolutions we have?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.410
There have been too many!
What a wild era this has been!

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:44.450
Here we go! Millionaire!
I have become king! Now bow before me!

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.410
Just like the French Revolution.
Off with their heads.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:48.580
Marie Antoinette!

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:49.790
I don't know her!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.950
Aren't there any bodyguards around?

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.910
Those fools are moving about in confusion.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:59.200
My only remaining card
is the strongest one, a three!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.660
I got them now!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.500
I suppose I have no choice.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.160
Revolution.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.200
I lose!

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.620
And so the evil is defeated.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.660
That's overly optimistic of you.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:12.040
Mya-ko, you're hilarious!

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.700
It's the end of her degenerate reign.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.370
She saved her last revolution
to hit me with it at the end.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.790
That's too sadistic.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:20.080
How regrettable.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.830
In terms of rules, there's no issues.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.910
I'm talking about your personality!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:27.080
In terms of the game,
I'd rather you call it my sportsmanship.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.870
First, I do not wish to hear
about personalities from you, Kono.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.080
You said it!

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.620
You've always had that side to you.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.000
--Respectfully, I have to ask,
just what do you mean by "that side"?

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.790
--We haven't become one after all.
--Respectfully, I have to ask,
just what do you mean by "that side"?

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.660
Wait just a second, you two!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:46.120
You're always acting like a robot,
and you don't understand people's feelings.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.040
You're the one without tact, Kono!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.620
What's that? Are ya callin' me boorish?

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.160
Seems like I've found a weak spot!

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.080
Now, now. Let's all settle down.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.830
This is absurd.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.500
It's totally fun!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:01.370
This game is over!
This card game is hereby dissolved!

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.250
That suits me just fine!

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.200
On what grounds? That's so uncool!

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:08.700
Seems like it's become
a legitimate presidential directive now.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.290
A fight, huh? I challenge you to a duel!

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:12.700
I accept that challenge.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.370
Don't say such stupid things!

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.250
What if you get bruised, huh?

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.080
Well, since you both lost...

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.950
--Shut your trap!
--Be quiet, Toda.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.620
--Scary!
--Um, everyone...

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:37.000
♪ The first star sparkled ♪

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:42.080
♪ The second star twinkled ♪

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:47.160
♪ The third star glittered ♪

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:53.330
♪ The fourth star dazzled ♪

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:56.910
Dummy, we can't lose even one of us.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:02.290
It's the eight of us that were gathered
to make up 22/7.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.080
Why are you saying
something so embarrassing?

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:27.370
Heave-ho...

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.000
Thanks for that.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.370
Why are you thanking me?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.540
It's not like you were the one fighting.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:47.080
I wanted... to say something.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:52.040
To be honest, you're the one
I've understood the least, Ayaka.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.330
Are you dissing me?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.620
Ah, sorry! That's not what I meant!

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:00.790
After all, you're...
the one I'm the least close with.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:05.660
You're so mature and smart and reliable.

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.080
It's normal for everyone to be different.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:10.750
We seem to be going in the same direction,

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.120
and I think to myself,
"Maybe we really are together."

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.950
After all, we won't really change.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.120
Neither you, Christer, nor me.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:21.120
Huh, me?

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.950
You hate someone. You love someone.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:33.330
They're reliable, or they're lazy,
smart or stupid, strong or weak...

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.330
...but we're really just cute girls?

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.870
I hope our one year anniversary
concert succeeds.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:42.750
Yeah!

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:46.330
--And we have work tomorrow, too.
--Yeah.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.660
I didn't think you--

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.500
S-Stop, Ayaka.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:50.750
It's fine, isn't it?

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.910
--Hold on--
--It's not like you'll lose anything.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:28.250
Man, 22/7 is great!
I'm definitely buying their new single.

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:32.040
--I want to go to their anniversary concert!
--I'm looking forward to it!

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.450
Jun, your sleeping posture was so bad!

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.700
You were snoring, Mya-ko.

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:39.660
I was not! I'm an idol!

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:42.370
The hot springs were so fun.

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:47.250
Yeah. This way, our feelings are refreshed, and
we can focus on doing our best for the concert.

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:50.500
It's here!

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:52.620
I wonder if this Order
is details about the concert.

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:54.120
Probably more outrageous stuff.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:57.200
Awesome!
Whatever comes, we'll overcome it!

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:01.000
At first, we were all uncertain
and didn't understand what was going on.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.080
But since we started
obeying the Wall's Orders,

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:06.200
we began to work together as a team.

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:09.620
22/7 became popular.

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:12.750
It was as if the Wall guided us
to nothing but good things.

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:17.250
I wonder what it is?

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:22.370
Jun? Did something happen?

00:23:24.410 --> 00:23:26.540
Jun?

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.870
I want to do a concert overseas next!

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:30.620
Overseas? Really?

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:31.870
You're getting too cocky.

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.750
No, no. Japan is far too small for 22/7!

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:37.370
I want to do a homecoming concert!

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:40.790
Reika?

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:43.830
What's up? Did something happen?

00:23:44.830 --> 00:23:45.910
What?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.040
"DISBAND."

00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:07.250
"Episode 10: Goodbye to Our World"

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:10.330
"Episode 10: Goodbye to Our World"

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:10.330
"Goodbye to Our World."
